{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":53753,"duration_api_ms":49705,"num_turns":10,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0f3a6c91-bd64-421b-abe4-b73d98f76e0b","total_cost_usd":0.4824585,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44358,"cache_read_input_tokens":321362,"output_tokens":1780,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44358,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":1780,"cacheReadInputTokens":321362,"cacheCreationInputTokens":44358,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4824585,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"evidence":["All 18 save_load tests pass, including the 3 new malformed-geometry regression tests (negative fill height, negative substrate depth, substrate depth exceeding fill height) and the shared assertion helper.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core --tests -- -D warnings` passes cleanly with no warnings.","`cargo fmt -p tank_core -- --check` passes with no formatting issues.","MigrationFn signature is `fn(&mut Value) -> Result<(), SimError>` (save.rs:33) with dedicated `SimError::SchemaMigration { from, to, message }` variant (actions.rs:82-83).","Compile-time assertion at save.rs:89-92 prevents MIGRATIONS length from drifting from SCHEMA_VERSION - MIN_SUPPORTED_SCHEMA.","Migration contract is well-documented at save.rs:41-76 with 5 numbered steps, 'what migrations can do' section, and 'ordering guarantees' section.","migrate_v2_to_v3 now uses `required_positive_f64_at` for length, width, and fill_height (save.rs:214-216), rejects negative substrate depths explicitly (save.rs:244-252), validates substrate_depth <= fill_height with tolerance (save.rs:256-264), and requires positive net water volume (save.rs:268-276).","The `required_positive_f64_at` helper (save.rs:386-401) correctly rejects values <= 0.0 with descriptive error messages including the path and actual value.","Scale computation is now a clean division `net_volume_l / gross_volume_l` (save.rs:278) with no silent clamping or zero fallback — all invalid cases are rejected before reaching this point.","Schema version is restamped after each migration step (save.rs:169), so a crash mid-chain leaves the save at a consistent intermediate version.","The `assert_schema_v2_migration_failure` helper (save_load.rs:304-325) is shared across all malformed-v2 tests, reducing duplication.","The only test failure in the full tank_core suite is `hatch_produces_juveniles` — a pre-existing regression from chemistry/nitrogen cycle changes, documented as outstanding risk in every prior stage output."],"findings_or_gaps":["The `hatch_produces_juveniles` shrimp population test still fails (adults=2, juveniles=0, TAN=2.169 mg/L). This is a pre-existing regression unrelated to the save-schema work, consistently documented across all prior stage outputs.","The pre-step `enforce_invariants(&mut self.state)` mutation-on-error architectural issue remains (pre-existing, unrelated to this deliverable).","The `substrate_depth > fill_height + 1e-9` tolerance check at save.rs:256 uses a hardcoded epsilon rather than a relative tolerance. For typical aquarium dimensions (cm-scale) this is perfectly adequate, but worth noting as a design choice."],"follow_up_or_amendments":["The `hatch_produces_juveniles` regression should be addressed in a separate task — either retune the test fixture or investigate excess ammonia accumulation in the nitrogen cycle.","The pre-step enforce_invariants mutation-on-error issue should be addressed separately by validating against a clone or splitting pure validation from normalization."],"outcome":"approved"},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d0335d22-307d-4afd-8a3b-ba50c005d0ab"}
